{"availability":"available","full":"Holmes-99/SecureVault","name":"SecureVault","description":"End-to-end encrypted file sharing over an untrusted server. AES-256-GCM, X25519, Ed25519, SHA-2 and HKDF implemented from scratch in Python, with a live MITM attacker demo. Applied Cryptography project, Birzeit University.","category":"Productivity","language":"Python","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-09-10T17:42:46Z","updated":"2026-10-06T19:28:39Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"","topics":["aes-256-gcm","applied-cryptography","argon2id","attacker","birzeit-university","cryptography","ed25519","end-to-end-encryption","gui","hkdf","python","safety-numbers","security","sha256","sha512","x25519"],"demo":"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1FTbIxETZ7RjuhxpHSZO8-puomnyNXUFB/view","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-17T02:59:21.139Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-17T02:59:21.139Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-17T02:59:21.139Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T18:25:28.739Z","stars":0,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-11T06:12:32.508Z","stars":0,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-17T02:59:21.139Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Encrypted document sharing on a server you don't trust.","Demo video · Design report · Design decisions · Slides","Our final project for ENCS4320 (Applied Cryptography) at Birzeit University."],"features":["All cryptography on the client. The server only stores and relays opaque bytes.","Cryptography written from scratch: SHA-256/512, HMAC, HKDF, AES-256, GCM, X25519 and Ed25519, tested against official NIST/RFC vectors and a reference library. Only Argon2id comes from a library.","No passwords on the server. Argon2id at 384 MiB, a salt per user, and a login challenge answered with HMAC.","Proof of origin. Every file is signed with Ed25519, and a third party can check the signature with no account and no server.","Key trust without a CA. Keys are pinned on first use and confi